nk is smooth and uniform dark brown (render-3), unlike the shaggy reddish-brown fibre in reference-1 and reference-2.", "No pendent fruit clusters appear in any render, although reference-0 shows them as a core trait. The owner notes fn-111 (date clusters) is not landed; this explains the absence but does not satisfy the trait."], "observations": ["Image order follows metadata: render-0 (seed 1, P-WHOLE), render-1 (seed 42, P-WHOLE), render-2 (seed 1, P-TRUNK), render-3 (seed 1, P-BASE), reference-0, reference-1, reference-2, anchor-0.", "Both renders show a single unbranched stem with near-constant diameter and a basal flare. There is no branching.", "Nothing grows on the trunk in either whole view. The knobs look like leaf-base stub organs (fn-110), not foliage or epiphytes.", "render-3 is marked visibility 'hidden' in the metadata, but the image clearly shows a close trunk section with a few knobs, so it was assessed as drawn.", "The reference trunk lean in reference-0 is a smooth lean or curve. The render kinks are abrupt zigzags, which is a different character. The owner priority explicitly forbids a wavy trunk.", "Finish quality (clean shading, shadows) is roughly comparable to the spruce anchor-0. The failures are morphological, not about finish.", "The epiphytic ferns in reference-1 and reference-2 are classed as variation. The owner requires a bare trunk, so their absence in the renders is correct."], "findings": [{"observation": "The crown is a short, thin starburst rather than a large rosette of long arching pinnate fronds with drooping lower fronds.", "evidence_ids": ["render-0", "render-1", "render-2", "reference-0", "reference-1"], "impact": "blocker", "uncertain": false, "causal_hypothesis": "Frond length and leaflet size dials may be too low, as the owner suggests; this is not established."}, {"observation": "Leaflets are tiny sparse chips, not long, narrow, stiff grouped leaflets.", "evidence_ids": ["render-2", "reference-1", "reference-2"], "impact